Here is how you can create a string parameter with a default value in Go:

```go
func greet(name string) {
    if name == "" {
        name = "Guest"
    }
    fmt.Println("Hello, " + name)
}
```

Alternatively, using a pointer to allow the caller to pass `nil` to use the default:

```go
func greet(name *string) {
    if name == nil {
        name = new(string)
        *name = "Guest"
    }
    fmt.Println("Hello, " + *name)
}
```

